      "summary": "Carmageddon rebuilt in C, function by function, from the original Windows 95 game.",
      "description": "Dethrace is a rebuild of Carmageddon, reverse-engineered from the original Windows 95 executable one function at a time and running natively on modern systems. Frontport builds it from source with SDL inside the app, because upstream’s Mac app expects SDL installed separately.\n\nThe game comes as a folder of files, or its zip. Frontport keeps a copy in the Port’s Data, where dethrace also keeps its options, key maps and saves, and settings such as Windowed = 1 go in dethrace.ini beside them. It accepts GOG’s Max Pack, which brings the CD music too, and the freeware demo from April 1997; the earlier demo from February doesn’t run. From GOG, add the installer you downloaded, setup_carmageddon_max_pack_1.0_gog_(77629).exe: Frontport unpacks it, and adds both Carmageddon and the Splat Pack. The first time, that builds the unpacker from source, which takes a few minutes.",
